## Lore

A few noro keep their race''s warrior heritage alive. Most of their people shun
them for it, and their answer is that a race without warriors risks
extermination. They turn considerable psionic power to combat and have developed
abilities that go past what mind melters and other psychics can do.

Many work for the CAF. Others are independent Bonded Deputies, bounty hunters or
outright vigilantes. Several have joined the rebellion against the Transgalactic
Empire, and a handful have become villains of the worst kind.

## Becoming one

Noro who feel the calling start developing offensive psionic powers in
adolescence. Families often suppress or discourage the signs, which as a rule
only makes the young noro keener to learn. A budding warrior who finds a teacher
develops powers no other class can - and is trained on the psionic power armour
the noro built.

## GM Notes

Mystic warriors often team up with cosmo-knights, phase adepts, undead slayers
and other champions of the forces of light. A few have travelled to other
dimensions, Rifts Earth among them, looking for a harder fight.

Cybernetics: none, and a mystic warrior will never consent to them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'noro-mystic-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
